    gist: 'Marriage is a legal contract, so it must meet set conditions to be valid in Ireland. Three months\' notice must be given to the Registrar before the ceremony. Both partners must be over 18, the marriage must be voluntary, both must be free to marry (not already married), and they must not be too closely related. On the day, two witnesses must be present, the register must be signed by the couple and witnesses, it must take place in a registered building (registry office, church or approved venue), and the marriage must be registered after the ceremony. Within marriage, a couple share responsibilities such as financial support for partner and children, joint guardianship of children, and providing for the children\'s physical, emotional, social, moral and educational needs.',
