    focus: 'Education\'s role + intrinsic vs extrinsic work satisfaction', level: 'higher',
    gist: 'Education has two big functions the exam returns to: it is a method of SOCIALISATION (formal learning in the classroom plus informal learning through the hidden curriculum — acceptable behaviour, cultural values, punctuality, respect for authority, sharing and teamwork) and it is PREPARATION FOR WORK (literacy and numeracy, formal qualifications, specialised skills and knowledge, plus personal qualities like responsibility and self-discipline; programmes such as TY, LCA and LCVP add a work-experience component). Attitude to WORK is shaped by two opposite drivers: intrinsic satisfaction comes from completing the work itself — work that is pleasant, fulfilling and challenging (linked to higher self-esteem and pride in the work) — while extrinsic satisfaction comes from the benefits around the job — high wages, a company car, bonuses, health insurance, time off — which can make repetitive or unfulfilling work worthwhile. Leisure adds the third strand, contributing to physical, social and emotional development.',
