    gist: 'A \'profile\' of a natural fibre is answered under three set headings: fibre production (how it is made), properties (what it is like to wear/use), and an identification (burn) test. The four natural fibres are cotton and linen (cellulose, from plants) and wool and silk (protein, from animals). Cotton comes from the boll/seed head of the cotton plant; linen from the stem of the flax plant (pulled, retted, crushed, combed, spun); wool is the sheared fleece of sheep; silk is unwound from the cocoon of the silkworm.',
