    focus: 'Blag / Giota Leanúnach (OL register)', level: 'ordinary',
    gist: 'At Ordinary Level you answer TWO of the four composition tasks (A, B, C, D), each worth 50 marks. The first task (A) is "Scríobh giota leanúnach nó blag" (a continuous piece or a blog), usually leathleathanach (about half a page) - so it is short and very winnable. The marking scheme splits each 50: An Tasc (did you actually write a blag/giota?) = 2, An tÁbhar (the content, linked to the title) = 8, and Cumas Gaeilge (your Irish) = 40. So 40 of the 50 are simply for good, accurate Irish - that is where you focus. The register of a blag is personal and informal, written in the chéad phearsa (first person, "mé/mo"): you are telling the reader about your own life. Open by setting it up - "Dia daoibh, a léitheoirí! Inniu tá mé chun scríobh faoi..." (Hi readers! Today I\'m going to write about...). Use simple linkers you are 100% sure of: "Ar dtús" (at first/firstly), "Ina dhiaidh sin" (after that), "Ar deireadh" (finally). Keep sentences short and correct rather than long and risky - the scheme rewards cruinneas (accuracy) and ticks every good phrase. The 2024 OL giota/blag titles were "Pearsa cheoil a thaitníonn go mór liom" (a music personality I really like), "Saol an scoláire sa séú bliain" (life of a sixth-year student), and "Eachtra a tharla i mo cheantar" (an event that happened in my area) - all invite your own real experience.',
