      text: 'At OL a 5-mark answer often pays 3 for the first correct piece and 2 for the second, and a shortened answer can drop. In the 2024 Blasket comprehension, \'Cén nós a bhíodh ag muintir an oileáin sna hoícheanta?\' → the full answer \'Bailiú le chéile i gceann de na tithe ag insint scéalta nó ag seinm ceoil\' = 5 mharc, but the half-answer \'Bailiú le chéile i gceann de na tithe\' (no mention of the storytelling/music) = only 3 mharc. So once you find the sentence that answers the question, copy the WHOLE thing — don\'t stop halfway.',
