    gist: 'Léamhthuiscint B works the same way as A, but the topic is denser (an intleacht shaorga = artificial intelligence) and the paragraphs are packed with facts, dates and names. Don\'t be intimidated by the téarmaíocht — the answers are still sitting in the named paragraph. Léigh an cheist, féach ar an alt atá luaite (Alt 1, Alt 2...), then scan that paragraph for the matching detail. Match the question word to the answer shape: \'Tabhair dhá chúis\' (give two reasons) needs TWO reasons; \'Luaigh dhá shampla\' (mention two examples) needs TWO examples; \'Cad a léiríonn...?\' (what shows...) wants the evidence the text gives. Glacfar le freagra i bhfocail an tsleachta for Ceist 1-5 — find it, lift it, score it. Note how the scheme marks these: the two-reason part (1a) is 3 marks split 2 + 1, and the two-example part (1b(i)) is 2 marks split 1 + 1 — so missing the second point always costs you. Ach Ceist 6(b) amháin: i d\'fhocail féin (your own words) — reword there.',
