      text: 'When a question says \'Scríobh síos dhá phíosa eolais...\' it is marked 3 + 2 = 5, so one fact (however good) caps you at 3. Count to two before you stop, and pick facts that don\'t overlap. For \'1.(b) Scríobh síos dhá phíosa eolais faoin bpáirt a ghlac Johnny i gcraobhchluiche sinsir scoileanna Chúige Laighean in 2002. (Alt 1)\' the answer sits in one sentence of Alt 1: \'Tháinig sé isteach sa chraobhchluiche sin mar ionadaí agus scóráil sé preabchúl trí nóiméad ó dheireadh an chluiche.\' That is two clean facts — he came on as a substitute (ionadaí) AND he scored a drop goal (preabchúl). Lift both. Find the alt, take the whole relevant line, in the passage\'s own Irish. (Contrast 1(a), a single 5-mark \'Cad?\' — there one correct fact, e.g. that his father and uncle were rugby players, already earns full marks.)',
